# A row that does not parse as the type inferred from earlier rows is DS3008 at the scan
# (LANGUAGE.md §3.1). Here `infer_rows = 1` infers `real` from the first row, and the third row
# holds `NA`.
mode: run
---- query
from read_csv('../../../data/options/semicolon.txt', delimiter = ';', quote = "'", header = false, infer_rows = 1)
---- expected
error[DS3008]: cannot read `../../../data/options/semicolon.txt`
  --> query:1:6
  |
1 | from read_csv('../../../data/options/semicolon.txt', delimiter = ';', quote = "'", header = false, infer_rows = 1)
  |      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ a value in this source does not match its column's type
  |
  = help: column types are inferred from the first rows of each file; `read_csv(..., infer_rows = n)` reads more rows to infer them
  = note: DataFusion said: Arrow error: Parser error: Error while parsing value 'NA' as type 'Float64' for column 2 at line 2. Row data: '[3,plain,NA]'
